pack.description=Resource Pack for cinema

mes_cnm.main_menu.text=§b§l- CinemaCraft Menu -%1%1§4§lCinema Mode%1§rEnables a mode where players can control camera functions and fly around the world for cinematic shots, offering full control over your perspective and movement.%1%1§4§lPathing Settings%1§rConfigure settings related to creating and editing paths for camera movement. Set predefined paths to ensure smooth, seamless camera transitions during your cinematic sequences.%1%1§4§lSaves%1§rView and manage different tracks created during the gameplay session. Tracks are predefined paths that the player has made, allowing you to review, adjust, or delete paths for perfect timing and composition.%1%1§4§lSettings%1§rAccess overall settings for the addon, allowing customization of various options to tailor your cinematic experience to your preferences.%1%1§4§lHelp/Infos%1§rClick to display help information in the chat, providing guidance on how to use the addon features. From here, you can access the key functions that enhance your cinematic experience.%1%1%1§b§lHotbar Items in Cinema Mode%1§rPlayers in Cinema Mode are switched to Adventure Mode and provided with special items to control the camera. These items give you the ability to customize your perspective and movement for optimal cinematic shots.%1%1§cPlay/Pause%1§rStarts or pauses the current movement type.%1%1§cMovement Type%1§rChanges how the player moves during Cinema Mode. Options include North, East, South, West, Up, Down, Head Rotation, and Focus Point Rotation.%1%1§cCamera Type%1§rChoose a different camera perspective. Options include Top, Right Shoulder, Left Shoulder, Isometric, Custom Offset, Custom Still, and Reset.%1%1§cPlace Focus Point%1§rPlaces a focus point in the world where the player is looking. Only one focus point can be active at a time. Placing another will remove the first.%1%1§cRemove Focus Point%1§rRemoves the currently placed focus point.%1%1§cShow/Hide Focus Point%1§rToggle the visibility of your focus point. This setting only affects points you have placed and does not impact other players.%1%1§cSpeed%1§rAdjust the camera movement speed. There are four speed options ranging from Slowest to Fastest.%1§b§lUsage Tips%1§rUse Show/Hide Points to manage the visibility of points you have placed, ensuring a clutter-free view while setting up shots. Experiment with different Camera Types to achieve various cinematic effects and perspectives.%1%1%1%1§b§lPath Mode%1§rPlayers in Path Mode are switched to Adventure Mode and equipped with items to control path mode functions, enabling smooth camera movement along pre-defined paths.%1%1§cPlay/Pause%1§rStarts or pauses the path traversal.%1%1§cRemove Path Points%1§rClears any path points that the player has placed, including the focus point.%1%1§cPlace Path Point%1§rPlaces a path point that the camera will travel through during a timelapse.%1%1§cPlace Focus Point%1§rPlaces a focus point in the world where the player is looking. Only one focus point can be active at a time. Placing another will remove the first.%1%1§cRemove Focus Point%1§rRemoves the currently placed focus point.%1%1§cShow/Hide Points%1§rToggle the visibility of your path points. This setting only affects points you have placed and does not impact other players.%1%1§cSpeed%1§rAdjust the camera movement speed. There are four speed options ranging from Slowest to Fastest.%1§b§lUsage Tips%1§rScroll through your hotbar to hide items and maintain a clear screen while setting up shots.%1Use Place Path Point and Place Focus Point strategically to create smooth and dynamic camera paths. Adjust the Speed settings to control the pace of your timelapse or cinematic shots.%1§2- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

mes_cnm.info.text=Follow us on §bTwitter @MonsterEggMC §rfor support, updates, and more! %1We're here to help you make the most of CinemaCraft!%1%1§4§lHow to Record Your Gameplay%1§rTo capture your CinemaCraft adventures, start your recording software before launching the add-on. %1Unfortunately, we can't control the recording process on consoles and PCs, so please manually start your recording software to capture your gameplay. %1Here are some ways to record on different consoles:%1%1§b§lXbox  %1§r%1Use the Xbox Game DVR feature.%1Press the Xbox button on your controller, then press the "X" button to record the last 30 seconds, or press the "View" button and select "Record from now" to start recording.%1%1§b§lPlayStation  %1§r%1Use the Share button on your controller.%1Press the Share button, then select "Start New Recording" or double-press the Share button to begin recording. Press the Share button again to stop recording.%1%1§b§lNintendo Switch  %1§r%1Use the Capture button on your left Joy-Con.%1Press and hold the Capture button to record the last 30 seconds of gameplay. For longer recordings, consider using a capture card connected to a PC.%1%1§b§lPC  %1§r%1For PC users, you can use software like OBS Studio, Bandicam, or the built-in recording features of your graphics card (e.g., NVIDIA ShadowPlay, AMD ReLive).%1

